# Tam Hobb, raking salt.
dialogue tamhobb
  node root tamhobb "New, are you? New ones stare at the salt like it owes them money."
    > "You're Tam Hobb." if not seen:tamhobb.tam -> tam
    > "He's on the Marrow. Your name's on his arm." if seen:tamhobb.tam and not seen:tamhobb.arm -> arm
    > "Your son's in Upper Town, counting ships off the wall." if seen:tam.dad and seen:tamhobb.tam and not seen:tamhobb.son -> son
    > "Any advice for a man with a Pike problem?" if not quill_free -> pike
    > "Back to the salt." -> bye
  node tam tamhobb "Who's asking? …No. Don't tell me. You've got paperwork in your face. And word gets round. You're the Fenn boy."
    > "He's on the Marrow. Your name's on his arm." -> arm
  node arm tamhobb "On his arm? In ink? (He leans on the rake, harder than a man needs to.) He'll have spelled it wrong."
    -> arm2
  node arm2 tamhobb "Tell my brother I said his tattoos are terrible."
    > "He put your name on his arm. The week you went." -> room
    > "I'll tell him. From a distance." -> distance
  node room tamhobb "…Course he did. Big soft lump. Tell him that too. No. Don't. I'll tell him."
  node distance tamhobb "Wise. He hugs like a capstan."
  node son narrator "The rake stops."
    -> son2
  node son2 tamhobb "Little Tam. He'll be ten. Counting ships. He gets that from me. I count everything here. Pans. Days. The buttons on Pike."
    > "He said to tell you he kept counting." if seen:tam.promise -> counting
    > "He's still got your cap. It's still too big." -> cap
  node counting tamhobb "Did he. (He looks at the salt for a while.) Then I'd better come home and be counted."
  node cap tamhobb "It was too big for me too. Tell him it fits eventually. Most things do, if you stop growing out of them."
  node pike tamhobb "Pike? Pike'd let the devil out if the devil had the right form. Trouble is, nobody's ever seen the right form. Not on this key."
  node bye tamhobb "Mind the pans. They're deeper than they look. Most things here are."
  # Act IV, in Upper Town, home.
  node home tamhobb "Clerk. I've been home an hour, and my wife has said my name eleven times. I'm counting. The boy taught me."
    > "And your brother?" -> brother
    > "You brought the rake." -> rake
    > "Goodnight, Tam." -> homebye
  node brother tamhobb "Down at the Keel, showing the whole room his arm. He isn't crossing my name out. He's writing HOME under it, in worse ink."
  node rake tamhobb "Three years. My hands don't know what to do without it. (He looks at it.) I'll hang it over the door. Pike can come and inspect it."
  node homebye tamhobb "Night, clerk. Mind the step. The boy says it's a killer. It's just a step."
